    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-73751",
      "knowledge_point_id": "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination",
      "problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-10y=-5 \\\\ 2x-4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=4$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=4,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution.",
